{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787821813207729752,"compiled_state":{"alias":"rapt-dreadable-dromedary","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"958ca4588d3939df46a50b0500193f9f38c2a39e50ddd328a9277461103781ad","event_uuid":"a0f50db4-7ef7-41f5-870d-e19557ac57fb","position":{"commit_sha":"864b01695293303f738c8acf263fcc916a69eddc","position":"1787815077692201001-a0f50db4-7ef7-41f5-870d-e19557ac57fb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"86ef4ed7f101d12fb1a7231a42b8eb0574c2593772624e96badd08a97d30aa8b","event_uuid":"aa3b3f42-5d08-46fb-8cf0-52abc44521a8","position":{"commit_sha":"3f47687ad0d688f597481519f6c21ffd8df24a2f","position":"1787815101410454001-aa3b3f42-5d08-46fb-8cf0-52abc44521a8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787815077692201001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aa3b3f42-5d08-46fb-8cf0-52abc44521a8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b3aa-b77b-cf87-4481"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`_reads._tracker` raises `store_uninitialized` only when the tracker directory is ABSENT\n(`src/rebar/_reads.py`, `if not os.path.isdir(tracker)`). A directory that EXISTS but is not a\nusable store — no `.git`, or a `.git` with no resolvable HEAD, or one mid-clone — satisfies\n`isdir`, so every read returns `[]`. The caller cannot distinguish \"this store is empty\" from\n\"this store is broken\", which is the exact confusion the guard was added to remove.\n\n## Encountered three times, each independently\n\n1. **In production.** The deployed MCP server served an EMPTY tracker for an extended period.\n   The store dir held `reviewbot-ensure-tickets` marker files and no `.git` at all; `isdir` was\n   true, so the guard never fired and `rebar.list_tickets()` returned `READ_OK count=0`. Proven\n   on the box before repair.\n2. **`fathomable-yester-thrip` (change 2244, merged).** `clear_tracker_dir` empties the\n   directory's CONTENTS but leaves the directory, so between the clear and a completed clone\n   reads return `[]`. Recorded there as a residual rather than fixed.\n3. **`unfit-beneficial-whimbrel` AC3.** \"While the clone is in flight, tracker reads report\n   `store_uninitialized` rather than `[]`\" — NOT met, for the same reason. That AC is\n   explicitly left unticked and points here.\n\n## Why the obvious fixes do not apply\n\nThe MCP deployment's tracker path is itself a MOUNT POINT (`/dev/nvme1n1`, xfs, verified in\n`/proc/mounts`), so the directory cannot be removed and nothing can be renamed over it — which\nis why the entrypoint clears contents rather than the directory. The fix has to be on the READ\nside.\n\n## Constraint the fix must respect\n\nAn EXISTING but empty INITIALIZED store must still read `[]` — that is a real contract with an\nexisting test (`tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py`: \"An EXISTING but empty store is\nNOT an error\"). So the discriminator cannot be emptiness. It has to be \"is this a usable\nstore\": rebar's own `.env-id` initialization marker and/or a resolvable git HEAD. Note the\nrelated inconsistency already filed as `ab61-f3e8-6ee6-4905` (`comment` succeeds without\n`.env-id` while `create` fails), which suggests `.env-id` is the intended marker.\n\n## Blast radius\n\n`_reads._tracker` funnels 7 read entry points, so this changes core read semantics repo-wide.\nThat is why it was scoped out of 2244 rather than folded in.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A tracker directory that exists but is NOT a usable store reads as `store_uninitialized`,\n      not `[]`.\n- [ ] An existing, empty, INITIALIZED store still reads `[]` — the existing contract test\n      continues to pass unmodified.\n- [ ] A store mid-clone (directory present, HEAD not yet resolvable) reads as uninitialized.\n- [ ] Regression coverage fails if the predicate reverts to a bare `os.path.isdir`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"aefe-614a-2631-4117","ticket_type":"bug","title":"reads return [] for a directory that exists but is not a usable store, so a broken store is indistinguishable from an empty one","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a0f50db4-7ef7-41f5-870d-e19557ac57fb","aa3b3f42-5d08-46fb-8cf0-52abc44521a8"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787821813207729752,"uuid":"db5e15c7-a92b-4cf4-a308-9bec16e9b82a"}